course: dictionary
lesson: 1800
title: Closer: nearer, or more careful
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Closer is the comparative of close, so it compares two things: one is nearer, or more connected, than the other. Look at the words around it to find which meaning it has. «Come closer, the puppy is shy» means nearer in distance.
explain: Closer can also mean nearer in time, or more friendly. «Closer to bedtime, the house went quiet» is about time. «They became closer friends» means they grew more connected, not that they stood nearer to each other.
explain: In maths, closer means nearer to the right answer. In science, a closer look means a more careful look. The sentence tells you which kind. Check the clues, then swap in "nearer" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Closer is the comparative of close: close, closer, closest.
fact: «Closer» can mean nearer in distance, nearer in time, more friendly, more careful, or nearer to a number.
fact: «Falcons look like hawks, but DNA ... shows they are closer cousins of parrots and songbirds.» Here closer means more closely related.
fact: «Fungi ... are in fact closer relatives of animals than of plants.» Closer again means more closely related.
fact: A good check is to swap in "nearer" or "more careful" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «Come closer, the puppy is shy.» In this sentence, closer means? | Later in time | Smaller in size | *Nearer in distance | More careful
exercise: «Your guess was closer than mine to the real number.» What does closer mean? | Slower to finish | *Nearer to the right answer | Taller and thinner | Louder than mine
exercise: «Take a closer look at the leaf under the magnifying glass.» What does closer mean? | Nearer in time | Less important | *More careful and exact | Quieter
test: «Closer to bedtime, the house went quiet.» Closer here means? | Nearer in distance | *Nearer in time | Nearer to a number | More friendly
test: «They became closer friends after the trip.» What does closer mean? | *More connected and friendly | Nearer in distance | More careful | Nearer to an answer
exam: «Falcons look like hawks, but they are closer cousins of parrots.» Closer here means? | Nearer in distance | Faster | *More closely related | Louder
